WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.366
During our heroes' journey to the Anistar City Gym,

2
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:08.366
where Ash hopes to win his seventh Kalos Gym Badge,

3
00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:10.466
they find themselves in a rainstorm.

4
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:13.766
Next stop? The Pokémon Centre.

5
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:17.233
Oh, we were really lucky there was a Pokémon Centre so close by.

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.700
- You got a little wet.
- Heh, yeah, but I'm OK.

7
00:00:20.766 --> 00:00:24.200
- How are you, Dedenne?
- Ne! Denne-ne!

8
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.200
I'll take care of Pikachu and your other Pokémon.

9
00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:30.233
You'll be back on your journey in no time.

10
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.366
Wigglytuff.

11
00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:34.100
- Thanks, Nurse Joy.
- Pika! Pika!

12
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.300
- Aw. Hmm.
- Ne!

13
00:00:39.966 --> 00:00:43.566
Aww, come on. Is this rain ever gonna stop?

14
00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:45.400
Denne-ne.

15
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.733
Perfect. Because the future is now, thanks to science.

16
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.833
Clemontic Gear, on.

17
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.300
I thought we'd encounter a situation precisely like this one.

18
00:00:56.366 --> 00:00:58.333
I call this the Weather Predictor.

19
00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:02.633
Not the most creative name I've heard.

20
00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:06.633
All right, I'll start collecting data right away.

21
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.133
I point it towards the sky.

22
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.900
Then it collects lots of data,

23
00:01:09.966 --> 00:01:13.200
like the movement of rainclouds, wind, humidity, and temperature,

24
00:01:13.266 --> 00:01:15.000
which it uses to predict the weather.

25
00:01:15.066 --> 00:01:17.500
Wow! Science is so amazing.

26
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:23.700
Uh, Clemont? When do you expect to have the results?

27
00:01:23.766 --> 00:01:25.300
Now let me see.

28
00:01:25.366 --> 00:01:28.466
It should take approximately one day to collect the data,

29
00:01:28.533 --> 00:01:30.333
but the results will be perfect.

30
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.733
- Uh...
- A whole day?

31
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.333
See, by then, it won't even be raining any more.

32
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.533
Hm, if I raise the analysis speed, maybe it'll work faster.

33
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.000
Now...

34
00:01:42.066 --> 00:01:43.700
-What's going on?

35
00:01:46.966 --> 00:01:49.133
It never fails to fail.

36
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.166
Back to the drawing board, big brother.

37
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.933
Denne-ne-ne.

38
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

39
00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:58.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

40
00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:02.066
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

41
00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.533
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

42
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.366
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

43
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:10.633
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

44
00:02:10.699 --> 00:02:14.066
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

45
00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:18.033
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

46
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.733
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

47
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.000
♪ Pokémon! ♪

48
00:02:29.366 --> 00:02:32.633
Adventures in Running Errands!

49
00:02:36.566 --> 00:02:38.600
- OK, here we go.
- Wigglytuff!

50
00:02:38.666 --> 00:02:41.300
- Yes.
- Pika! Pi!

51
00:02:41.366 --> 00:02:43.800
How're you feeling, buddy?

52
00:02:43.866 --> 00:02:46.300
Everyone's feeling perfectly fine.

53
00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.300
Thank you so much, Nurse Joy. Great.

54
00:02:52.166 --> 00:02:53.300
Ne!

55
00:02:53.366 --> 00:02:54.900
It's still coming down.

56
00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:57.366
Why don't we just hang out here a little bit longer?

57
00:02:57.433 --> 00:02:58.866
That's a good idea.

58
00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.800
-What's going on here?

59
00:03:13.866 --> 00:03:16.733
- What happened?
- It's a blackout.

60
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.600
- Everybody, stay calm.
- Wiggly! Wigglytuff! Tuff!

61
00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:24.066
We've got a problem.

62
00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:28.000
- What's going on, Nurse Joy?
- None of the equipment is working.

63
00:03:28.066 --> 00:03:29.466
Huh? That's bad.

64
00:03:29.533 --> 00:03:31.900
There may be a problem with the main system.

65
00:03:31.966 --> 00:03:34.300
Would it be all right if I go and have a look?

66
00:03:34.366 --> 00:03:37.300
- Sure. This way.
- Wigglytuff. Wigglytuff!

67
00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:44.766
In here.

68
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.266
-Pika.

69
00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.833
It looks to me like that leak caused a short circuit.

70
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.566
- A short circuit?
- You mean it's broken?

71
00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:57.800
-What do I do?

72
00:03:57.866 --> 00:04:00.866
I'm still in the middle of treating several Pokémon.

73
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:01.900
Wigglytuff.

74
00:04:01.966 --> 00:04:04.533
Clemont. Do you think you can fix that?

75
00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.400
- Do you?
- Just a minute.

76
00:04:08.466 --> 00:04:12.666
Hmm, so it's a type 002. I can do this.

77
00:04:12.733 --> 00:04:16.399
- Let's give it a try.
- Oh, would you? Thanks.

78
00:04:16.466 --> 00:04:20.266
Just leave it to me. I'm pretty good at repairing things.

79
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:24.966
So let's let Clemont handle this and we'll do whatever we can to help him out.

80
00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:29.300
OK. Since the Pokémon Centre is without power, people will need help.

81
00:04:29.366 --> 00:04:31.766
I wanna help too. Yay!

82
00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:35.500
- Thanks to all of you. You're sweet.
- Tuff!

83
00:04:35.566 --> 00:04:39.166
First we're gonna have to figure out how to stop that leak.

84
00:04:39.233 --> 00:04:41.533
I'll go up and have a look at the roof, OK?

85
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.666
But, Ash, it's still pouring rain.

86
00:04:43.733 --> 00:04:45.500
- Be careful.
- Right.

87
00:04:45.566 --> 00:04:49.200
Of course. Now, why didn't I think of that before?

88
00:04:49.266 --> 00:04:50.733
Luxray.

89
00:04:52.566 --> 00:04:53.833
Lux.

90
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.900
Luxray and Pikachu can produce enough power to run the Pokémon Centre.

91
00:04:57.966 --> 00:05:02.233
Then the system should be able to function for at least a little while.

92
00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.066
- Think you can do it, buddy?
- Pika!

93
00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:08.100
- Hey. Dedenne can help too. Will you?
- Huh?

94
00:05:08.233 --> 00:05:10.000
I'm sure you'll be great.

95
00:05:10.066 --> 00:05:11.066
Denne, denne!

96
00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:12.433
Dedenne wants to help out.

97
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.600
We're all set. Go ahead.

98
00:05:18.666 --> 00:05:21.400
- Ray!
- Chu!

99
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:24.800
Ne... Denne!

100
00:05:32.866 --> 00:05:36.866
- We're up and running.
- Pikachu, Luxray and Dedenne.

101
00:05:36.933 --> 00:05:40.133
- Keep up the good work.
- You can do it.

102
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.200
- Pika!
- Good luck.

103
00:05:42.266 --> 00:05:43.800
Thanks. I'll do my best.

104
00:05:43.866 --> 00:05:45.333
I'm terribly sorry.

105
00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.833
All of our healing equipment is down right now.

106
00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:51.800
But these berries can help. So please, take whatever you need.

107
00:05:51.866 --> 00:05:53.800
Wigglytuff.

108
00:05:53.866 --> 00:05:55.733
- You need an Oran Berry.
- Aah! Heh.

109
00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:56.900
Wigglytuff.

110
00:05:56.966 --> 00:05:59.533
Nurse Joy? Would you let us help you out with this?

111
00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.866
That would be wonderful.

112
00:06:00.933 --> 00:06:04.866
I need to go check on a Pokémon who's in need of some special treatment.

113
00:06:04.933 --> 00:06:07.866
- Sure.
- Leave it to us.

114
00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.966
Come on out, Braixen and Pancham.

115
00:06:11.033 --> 00:06:12.466
- Braix.
- Cham.

116
00:06:12.533 --> 00:06:15.466
Everybody, form a line here.

117
00:06:15.533 --> 00:06:17.466
Cham, Pancham.

118
00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:26.000
Hm?

119
00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:29.066
There it is.

120
00:06:34.466 --> 00:06:37.066
OK. Hawlucha!

121
00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:38.533
Lucha!

122
00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.033
Frogadier.

123
00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.466
Froga!

124
00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:45.366
'Kay, I've gotta fix the roof. Do you think you two can help me out?

125
00:06:45.433 --> 00:06:46.633
Cha-la.

126
00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:50.500
OK, first, make us some Frubbles, because it's pretty slippery.

127
00:06:50.566 --> 00:06:52.900
Frogadier!

128
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.233
Awesome. Thanks, Frogadier.

129
00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.533
- Ha!
- Dier!

130
00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.866
Lu.

131
00:07:02.933 --> 00:07:08.366
- Hm. I need you to hold this for me. OK?
- Cha.

132
00:07:08.433 --> 00:07:11.733
Now, Frogadier, check to see if there are any more holes, 'kay?

133
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:12.800
Gadier.

134
00:07:15.766 --> 00:07:17.333
Braix.

135
00:07:18.366 --> 00:07:20.433
Jigglypuff!

136
00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.433
- Pika, pika!
- Ray!

137
00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:32.833
How is it going?

138
00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.733
- Bunnelby.
- Pika.

139
00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.200
- Ray.
- Is there anything I can get for you?

140
00:07:37.266 --> 00:07:39.200
- Yes, this.
- Huh?

141
00:07:39.266 --> 00:07:42.466
This fuse isn't working any more and needs to be replaced.

142
00:07:42.533 --> 00:07:45.533
- Do you happened to have a spare?
- Hm.

143
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.733
I don't, but I think there might be a shop nearby.

144
00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:51.166
So that means I'll have to go get another one.

145
00:07:51.233 --> 00:07:53.000
I wish I could help.

146
00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.733
- Uh-oh. Another short.

147
00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.400
I've gotta get this fixed as soon as possible. Aah! Aah!

148
00:08:01.466 --> 00:08:02.633
Aaaah!

149
00:08:02.733 --> 00:08:04.066
- Chespin!
- Huh?

150
00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:05.933
- Chespin.
- Che.

151
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
- Pika?
- Luxray.

152
00:08:08.066 --> 00:08:09.433
Bunnelby?

153
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.400
Chespin. Che, Chespin.

154
00:08:11.466 --> 00:08:15.033
Wow, that would be great if you can go and get that fuse for me.

155
00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.566
Che. Che!

156
00:08:16.633 --> 00:08:19.333
I'm counting on you. Thanks a lot.

157
00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:22.966
- Please go and get it as soon as you can.
- Pin.

158
00:08:23.033 --> 00:08:24.033
Bunnelby?

159
00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.766
Bunnelby?

160
00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:28.800
Will you go with Chespin for me?

161
00:08:28.866 --> 00:08:31.633
- Bunnelby!
- Che!

162
00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.366
Bunn!

163
00:08:34.433 --> 00:08:36.900
- Pika, pika.
- Luxray, ray.

164
00:08:39.433 --> 00:08:42.733
- Looks like the rain's finally stopped.
- Chespin!

165
00:08:42.799 --> 00:08:45.366
- Che.
- Hey, wait a second.

166
00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:50.600
Here. I've written down what I need on this piece of paper.

167
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:53.800
Please show it to the shopkeeper. OK?

168
00:08:56.233 --> 00:08:57.433
Pin, pin.

169
00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.866
The shop is right down that path.

170
00:08:59.933 --> 00:09:03.133
There are no turns, so you can't get lost. Got it?

171
00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.133
- Chespin, che.
- Bunnel.

172
00:09:06.066 --> 00:09:07.733
Chespin!

173
00:09:09.033 --> 00:09:11.566
Don't forget. Stay on the path.

174
00:09:11.633 --> 00:09:14.366
Where are Chespin and Bunnelby going?

175
00:09:14.433 --> 00:09:18.233
- I sent them out on an errand.
- Wow, good for them.

176
00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.800
Hey, you two. Good luck.

177
00:09:20.866 --> 00:09:22.466
- Bunnelby!
- Chespin!

178
00:09:22.533 --> 00:09:25.966
That's that. I guess I'd better finish up a little bit more work

179
00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:27.566
before they get back.

180
00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:29.833
